 faq=[('Where should I start?','Start free. If you want programming fundamentals, open Python. For architecture and tradeoffs, open System Design. To find a particular topic, search the library.'),('What is inside the library?','Programming notes, system design, database references, developer tools, algorithms, handwritten PDFs, and Python notebooks. Everything comes from the existing Notex collection.'),('Is this only for interview prep?','No. Use the notes as a practical reference, work through examples, or follow your own curiosity. The interview study plan is one part of the collection.'),('Can I use it without paying?','Yes. All notes, notebooks, and PDFs are free. No account or subscription is needed.'),('Can I contribute a correction?','Yes. Use Edit on GitHub on a note, or open an issue in the repository. Notex is built in the open.'),('Where do my saved notes go?','They stay in this browser on your device. Open a note and select Save note, then use the Saved filter in the library.')]
